/*  Emitting C — the checked program, one statement at a time, as C that calls the runtime
    (`cufet-runtime.h`, the one `cufet build` links).

    ★ Held to what the program PRINTS, not to the C `CodeGenerator` writes (the user's ruling): the
    C here may differ from it freely, and each program built is run and compared with the
    interpreter.

    ★★ `unsupported` rather than a guess. Anything this compiler cannot build yet fails with
    `unsupported\t<what>`, never with C that might print the right thing — the same claim the
    checker makes with its own `unsupported`.

    ★ The tree carries no types, so the emitter keeps its own: the kind of each name it has defined,
    and from those the kind of each expression — as `TypeOf` does in `CodeGenerator`.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object emitter with (the map from text to text kinds, the chase body, the text indent,
        the map from text to node functions, the map from text to node objects, the map from text to node methods,
        the map from text to node interfaces, the map from text to fact specialized,
        the series of node pending-functions, the series of text pending-names,
        the series of map from text to text pending-kinds, the map from text to fact unions,
        the series of text union-order, the map from text to text constants,
        the map from text to fact constant-places, the map from text to fact kept-rabbits,
        the series of text lambda-types, the series of text lambda-protos, the series of text lambda-code,
        the map from text to text inferred, the map from text to node grouped).

    /// An emitter for the program, knowing its functions, objects, methods — a method under
    /// `<object>'s <method>` — and interfaces by name.
    Bind emitter to fresh-emitter, given (the map from text to node functions, the map from text to node objects,
            the map from text to node methods, the map from text to node interfaces):
        Return a new emitter { the kinds a map from text to text, the body a chase, the indent "    ",
            the functions functions, the objects objects, the methods methods, the interfaces interfaces,
            the specialized a map from text to fact, the pending-functions a series of node,
            the pending-names a series of text, the pending-kinds a series of map from text to text,
            the unions a map from text to fact, the union-order a series of text,
            the constants a map from text to text, the constant-places a map from text to fact,
            the kept-rabbits a map from text to fact, the lambda-types a series of text,
            the lambda-protos a series of text, the lambda-code a series of text, the inferred a map from text to text,
            the grouped a map from text to node }.
    Done.

    /// An emitter for another body of the same program — every table shared, the copies asked for
    /// included, so a copy one body asks for is built once for all of them.
    Bind emitter to sibling unto emitter:
        Return a new emitter { the kinds a map from text to text, the body a chase, the indent "    ",
            the functions one's functions, the objects one's objects, the methods one's methods,
            the interfaces one's interfaces, the specialized one's specialized,
            the pending-functions one's pending-functions, the pending-names one's pending-names,
            the pending-kinds one's pending-kinds, the unions one's unions, the union-order one's union-order,
            the constants one's constants, the constant-places one's constant-places,
            the kept-rabbits one's kept-rabbits, the lambda-types one's lambda-types,
            the lambda-protos one's lambda-protos, the lambda-code one's lambda-code, the inferred one's inferred,
            the grouped one's grouped }.
    Done.

    /// What this compiler cannot build yet, as a failure message.
    Bind text to not-built, given (the text what):
        Return "unsupported\t{what}".
    Done.

    /// A Cufet name as a C one: hyphens become underscores, which no Cufet name holds, behind a
    /// prefix that keeps it clear of C's own words.
    Bind text to c-name, given (the text name):
        Return "cv_" joined to cast c-ident on (name).
    Done.

    /// A function's name as C — a prefix of its own, so no value's name can ever meet it.
    Bind text to c-function-name, given (the text name):
        Return "cfn_" joined to cast c-ident on (name).
    Done.

    /// The kind of value a written type stands for, or "void" for none.
    Bind text or failure to kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        If cast is-nothing on (written), return "void".
        If written's kind is "NumberType", return "number".
        If written's kind is "TextType", return "text".
        If written's kind is "FactType", return "fact".
        If written's kind is "BitsType", return "bits".
        If written's kind is "ReadableStreamType", return "readable stream".
        If written's kind is "ChannelType":
            Define carried as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Return "channel of {carried}".
        Done.
        If written's kind is "WritableStreamType", return "writable stream".
        If written's kind is "SetType":
            Define member-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's set-kind-of-element on (member-kind) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If written's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define object-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (written, 1)).
            If (the entry for object-name in one's objects) is not void, return "object {object-name}".
            If (the entry for object-name in one's interfaces) is not void, return "interface {object-name}".
            // The prelude's rabbit: a region, carried as its name alone, as the interpreter's is.
            If object-name is "rabbit", return "rabbit".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {object-name}")).
        Done.
        If written's kind is "UnionType":
            // An open catalogue's cases are every kind the whole program ever puts in one, which
            // `CodeGenerator` gathers in a pass of its own over everything first; this compiler has none.
            If cast is-open-union on (written), return a failure (cast not-built on ("an open catalogue")).
            Define cases as a series of text.
            For each inner in (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s children, repeat:
                Define case-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (inner) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-scalar on (case-kind) is false and cast object-of on (case-kind) is "" and cast is-union on (case-kind) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a union holding a {case-kind}")).
                Done.
                Insert case-kind into cases.
            Done.
            Define union as cast union-kind-of on (cases).
            Cast one's register-union on (union).
            Return union.
        Done.
        If written's kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-scalar on (inner) is false and cast object-of on (inner) is "" and cast is-union on (inner) is false
                    and cast element-of on (inner) is "" and cast is-map on (inner) is false and cast is-record on (inner) is false
                    and inner is not "bits" and inner is not "address":
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a voidable {inner}")).
            Done.
            Cast one's register-union on ("voidable {inner}").
            Return "voidable {inner}".
        Done.
        If written's kind is "SeriesType":
            Define element as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            // A series of series: the inner series' type is written with the generated ones, after
            // whatever it holds.
            If (cast element-of on (element) is not "" or cast is-voidable on (element)) and cast is-element-kind on (element):
                Cast one's register-series on (element).
            Done.
            If cast is-element-kind on (element), return "series of {element}".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a series of {element}")).
        Done.
        If written's kind is "MapType":
            Define key-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define held as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's map-kind-of-type on (key-kind, held) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If written's kind is "RecordType", return cast one's record-kind-of-type on (written) or pass the failure off.
        If written's kind is "FailureType", return cast one's failable-kind-of-type on (written) or pass the failure off.
        If written's kind is "ChaseType", return "chase".
        If written's kind is "MatrixType", return "matrix".
        If written's kind is "AddressType", return "address".
        If written's kind is "AxiomType", return cast one's axiom-kind-of-type on (written) or pass the failure off.
        If written's kind is "FunctionType", return cast one's function-kind-of-type on (written) or pass the failure off.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {written's kind}")).
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A number as the runtime builds one: its digits, how many of them follow the point, its sign.
    Bind text or failure to number-literal, given (the text written):
        Define sign as 0.
        Define unsigned as written.
        If unsigned starts with "-":
            The sign becomes 1.
            The unsigned becomes the characters from 2 to the end of unsigned.
        Done.
        Define scale as 0.
        Define dot as (the position of "." in unsigned but void is 0).
        If dot is greater than 0, the scale becomes the length of unsigned - dot.
        Define digits as replace "." with "" in unsigned.
        // Written without its leading zeros, which C would read as octal — and split across two
        // 64-bit words, the high one what is left after the low one is taken out.
        Define coefficient as digits converted to number but void is 0.
        Define word-size as 18446744073709551616.
        Define over as coefficient / word-size.
        Define high-word as over - over % 1.
        Define low-word as coefficient - high-word * word-size.
        Return "cufet_dec_lit({high-word}ULL, {low-word}ULL, {scale}, {sign})".
    Done.

    /// The kind of value an expression gives: "number", "text", "fact", or "series of" one of them.
    Bind text or failure to kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "NumberLiteral", return "number".
            "StringLiteral" or "TextJoin" or "TextConvert", return "text".
            "BooleanLiteral", return "fact".
            "VariableReference":
                If cast standard-stream-kind on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1))) is not "":
                    Return cast standard-stream-kind on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1))).
                Done.
                Define reached as cast one's narrowed-read on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If the number of reached is 2, return item 1 of reached.
                Define known as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) in one's kinds.
                // A shared constant is seen from anywhere.
                If known is void, the known becomes the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) in one's constants.
                // A function of the program's own, named where a value goes.
                If known is void:
                    Define named-function as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) in one's functions.
                    If named-function is not void, return cast one's bound-kind on (named-function) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                If known is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the name '{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1))}', defined where this compiler cannot see it")).
                Return known.
            Done.
            "UnaryExpression":
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "Not":
                    // `not` on bits flips every bit, and is bits.
                    If (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off) is "bits", return "bits".
                    Return "fact".
                Done.
                Return "number".
            Done.
            "BinaryExpression":
                Define reached as cast one's overload-for on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If reached is not void, return cast one's overload-gives on (reached) or pass the failure off.
                If (cast one's is-matrix-binary on (expression) or pass the failure off), return cast one's matrix-binary-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
                If (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off) is "bits":
                    Return cast bits-binary-kind on (operator).
                Done.
                If operator is "Plus" or operator is "Minus" or operator is "Star" or operator is "Slash" or operator is "Percent":
                    Return "number".
                Done.
                Return "fact".
            Done.
            // Inside a `Try`, a call that can fail reads as its value.
            "CastExpression":
                // An axiom run by its name gives what its declaration says, and cannot fail.
                Define axiom as cast keyed-field on (expression, ":RunsAxiom").
                If axiom is not void, return cast one's axiom-result-kind on (axiom) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on (cast one's call-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off).
            Done.
            "AxiomLiteral", return cast one's axiom-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ForeignTextAt":
                Cast one's register-union on ("voidable text").
                Return "voidable text".
            Done.
            "ObjectLiteral":
                Define object-name as cast literal-object-name on (expression).
                If (the entry for object-name in one's objects) is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a new {object-name}")).
                Return "object {object-name}".
            Done.
            "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's possessive-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "SeriesLiteral" or "RangeExpression" or "SeriesLength" or "SeriesAccess":
                Return cast one's series-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "IsTypeCheck", return "fact".
            "VoidLiteral", return "void".
            "ButVoidDefault", return cast one's but-void-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "MapLiteral" or "MapLookup" or "MapHasKey" or "MapHasEntry" or "RecordNamedAccess":
                Return cast one's map-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "RecordLiteral", return cast one's record-literal-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ProgramArgumentsExpression", return "series of text".
            "ChaseLiteral", return "chase".
            "LambdaLiteral", return cast one's lambda-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ConditionalExpression", return cast one's chosen-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "UnburyExpression", return cast one's kind-of on (cast as-resumed on (expression)) or pass the failure off.
            "BitsLiteral" or "BitsShift" or "BitsConvert" or "BitsAtWidth", return "bits".
            "SetLiteral" or "SetHasMember", return cast one's set-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "MatrixLiteral" or "MatrixSized" or "MatrixAccess", return cast matrix-kind-of on (expression).
            "ReadExpression", return cast stream-read-kind on (expression).
            "ChannelCreation":
                Define carried as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Return "channel of {carried}".
            Done.
            "InterruptRequestedExpression", return "fact".
            "DeliveryExpression":
                Define from-channel as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Define delivered as "voidable {cast channel-element on (from-channel)}".
                Cast one's register-union on (delivered).
                Return delivered.
            Done.
            "AwaitedResultExpression":
                Define task-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-task-handle on (task-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("awaiting a {task-kind}")).
                // Inside a `Try`, a task that can fail reads as its value, as a call that can does.
                Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on (cast task-result on (task-kind)).
            Done.
            // `converted to number` cannot fail from bits — 64 bits always fit — and may from text.
            "NumberConvert":
                If (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off) is "bits", return "number".
                Return "voidable number".
            Done.
            "SortExpression", return cast one's sorted-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Otherwise:
                If cast is-random-expression on (kind), return cast one's random-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-text-operation on (kind), return cast text-operation-kind on (kind).
                If cast is-failure-expression on (kind), return cast one's failure-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The kind a call gives back, as its function declares it.
    Bind text or failure to call-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        If (cast one's calls-value on (expression) or pass the failure off):
            Return cast function-gives on (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off).
        Done.
        If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define method as cast one's method-called on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (method, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
            If (the entry for cast call-target on (expression) in one's functions) is void:
                Define by-argument as cast one's method-by-argument on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (by-argument, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define called as cast one's function-called on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (called, 2)) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// An expression as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "NumberLiteral", return cast number-literal on ((cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word) or pass the failure off.
            // The tree writes a text with C's own escapes, quotes and all.
            "StringLiteral", return (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
            "BooleanLiteral":
                If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "true", return "1".
                Return "0".
            Done.
            "VariableReference":
                Cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
                If cast standard-stream-kind on (name) is not "", return cast standard-stream-c on (name).
                If (the entry for name in one's kinds) is void and (the entry for name in one's constants) is void and (the entry for name in one's functions) is not void:
                    Return cast one's c-named-function on (name) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                // A narrowed name reads as its case, or as the smaller union.
                Define reached as cast one's narrowed-read on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If the number of reached is 2, return item 2 of reached.
                // A captured one, `one` included, through the environment it was captured into.
                Define redirected as the entry for "@{name}" in one's kinds but void is "".
                If redirected is not "", return redirected.
                // Inside a method, `one` is the object it was called on, held by its address.
                If name is "one", return "(*cv_one)".
                Return cast c-name on (name).
            Done.
            "ObjectLiteral", return cast one's c-object-literal on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "UnburyExpression", return cast one's c-of on (cast as-resumed on (expression)) or pass the failure off.
            "BitsLiteral" or "BitsShift" or "BitsConvert" or "BitsAtWidth", return cast one's c-bits-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "SetLiteral" or "SetHasMember", return cast one's c-set-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "MatrixLiteral" or "MatrixSized" or "MatrixAccess", return cast one's c-matrix-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ReadExpression", return cast one's c-read on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ChannelCreation", return cast one's c-channel on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "InterruptRequestedExpression", return "(cufet_interrupted ? 1 : 0)".
            "DeliveryExpression", return cast one's c-delivery on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "AwaitedResultExpression", return cast one's c-awaited on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's c-possessive on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "TextJoin":
                Define joined-left as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Define joined-right as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Define sides as a series of text with (joined-left, joined-right).
                Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2)), sides).
                Return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_concat({item 1 of sides}, {item 2 of sides})").
            Done.
            "TextConvert", return cast one's c-text-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            "UnaryExpression":
                Define operand as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word.
                If operator is "Minus", return "cufet_neg({operand})".
                If operator is "Not" and (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off) is "bits":
                    Return "cufet_bits_not({operand})".
                Done.
                If operator is "Not", return "(!{operand})".
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator}")).
            Done.
            "BinaryExpression", return cast one's c-binary on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "AxiomLiteral", return cast one's c-axiom-value on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ForeignTextAt", return cast one's c-text-at on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "CastExpression":
                If (cast keyed-field on (expression, ":RunsAxiom")) is not void, return cast one's c-axiom-call on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Define called-c as cast one's c-call on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (called-c, cast one's call-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off).
            Done.
            "SeriesLiteral" or "RangeExpression" or "SeriesLength" or "SeriesAccess":
                Return cast one's c-series-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "IsTypeCheck", return cast one's c-type-check on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            // `void` has no C of its own: it is made into the voidable it goes into.
            "VoidLiteral", return "0".
            "ButVoidDefault", return cast one's c-but-void on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "MapLiteral" or "MapLookup" or "MapHasKey" or "MapHasEntry" or "RecordNamedAccess":
                Return cast one's c-map-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "RecordLiteral", return cast one's c-record-literal on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "ChaseLiteral", return "cufet_chase_new()".
            "LambdaLiteral":
                Define lambda-label as "{(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word}_{(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word}".
                Return cast one's c-closure on (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2), "", "?", lambda-label) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "ConditionalExpression", return cast one's c-chosen on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            "SortExpression", return cast one's c-sorted on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            // From 1: argument zero is the program's own name, which no two ways of running it agree on.
            "ProgramArgumentsExpression":
                Return "(\{ cser_text* cf_args = cser_text_new(); for (int cf_ai = 1; cf_ai < cufet_argc; cf_ai++) cser_text_append(cf_args, (const char*)cufet_argv[cf_ai]); cf_args; \})".
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                If cast is-random-expression on (kind), return cast one's c-random-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-text-operation on (kind), return cast one's c-text-operation on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-failure-expression on (kind), return cast one's c-failure-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
                Return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The field a tree leaves after a key such as `:ResolvedTypeName`, or void when it has none.
    Bind voidable node to keyed-field, given (the node whole, the text key):
        Define place as 0.
        For each part in whole's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If part's word is key and place is less than the number of whole's children, return item (place + 1) of whole's children.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    /// The name a call reaches its function by: the filled-in copy the checker chose for a function
    /// with a blank, or the name written.
    Bind text to call-target, given (the node call):
        Define resolved as cast keyed-field on (call, ":ResolvedFunctionName").
        If resolved is not void, return cast unquoted on (resolved).
        Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (call, 1), 1)).
    Done.

    /// The function a call reaches — one of the program's own, called by its name.
    Bind node or failure to function-called unto emitter, given (the node call):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (call, 1).
        If callee's kind is not "VariableReference":
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of a {callee's kind}")).
        Done.
        Define called as the entry for cast call-target on (call) in one's functions.
        If called is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of something other than the program's own function")).
        Return called.
    Done.

    /// A call as C: the function's name and its arguments, in order.
    Bind text or failure to c-call unto emitter, given (the node call):
        If (cast one's calls-value on (call) or pass the failure off), return cast one's c-value-call on (call) or pass the failure off.
        If (cast field-of on (call, 1))'s kind is "PossessiveAccess", return cast one's c-method-call on (call) or pass the failure off.
        If (cast field-of on (call, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
            If (the entry for cast call-target on (call) in one's functions) is void:
                Cast one's method-by-argument on (call) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's c-method-call on (cast as-method-call on (call)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define called as cast one's function-called on (call) or pass the failure off.
        Define handed-c as cast one's c-arguments on (cast field-of on (called, 3), cast field-of on (call, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define listing as item 2 of handed-c.
        Define interface-taking as cast one's takes-interface on (called) or pass the failure off.
        If interface-taking:
            Define copy-name as cast one's c-specialized-name on (called, call) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast in-order on (item 1 of handed-c, "{copy-name}({listing})").
        Done.
        Return cast in-order on (item 1 of handed-c, "{cast c-function-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (called, 1)))}({listing})").
    Done.

    // ── Working operands out in order ─────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // ★ C leaves the order of a call's arguments open — gcc works them out last first — while the
    // interpreter goes left to right. So where two or more operands could do something, each is
    // bound to a temporary first, in the order written. A literal or a plain name stays in place:
    // no call can change a local, since a closure captures a snapshot.
    //
    // ★ The temporaries are named by place, `cf_o1`, `cf_o2`…: an operand's own temporaries live in
    // a block of their own inside it, so the same names nested cannot meet.

    /// Whether it cannot matter when an operand is worked out.
    Bind fact to is-order-free, given (the node operand):
        Define kind as operand's kind.
        Return kind is "NumberLiteral" or kind is "StringLiteral" or kind is "BooleanLiteral" or kind is "VoidLiteral"
            or kind is "VariableReference".
    Done.

    /// What binds the operands that need it to temporaries, in order — "" when fewer than two do.
    /// Each one bound is swapped for its temporary in `emitted`.
    Bind text to order-prefix, given (the series of node operands, the series of text emitted):
        Define busy as 0.
        For each operand in operands, repeat:
            If cast is-order-free on (operand) is false, increment busy by 1.
        Done.
        If busy is less than 2, return "".
        Define prefix as "".
        Define place as 0.
        For each operand in operands, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If cast is-order-free on (operand) is false:
                The prefix becomes "{prefix}__auto_type cf_o{place} = {item place of emitted}; ".
                Item place of emitted becomes "cf_o{place}".
            Done.
        Done.
        Return prefix.
    Done.

    /// What was built from the temporaries, inside the block that binds them.
    Bind text to in-order, given (the text prefix, the text built):
        If prefix is "", return built.
        Return "(\{ {prefix}{built}; \})".
    Done.

    /// A statement built from the temporaries, in a block of its own that binds them first.
    Bind text to in-order-statement, given (the text prefix, the text built):
        If prefix is "", return built.
        Return "\{ {prefix}{built} \}".
    Done.

    /// The operands of a node, fields `first` to `last`, as C — what binds them in order (see
    /// `order-prefix`), then each one's C. ★ The interpreter works a node's operands out in the
    /// order its fields come, which is not always the order written: `replace a with b in t` and
    /// `the characters from a to b of t` work out `t` first, and `the entry for k in m` works out `m`.
    /// ⚠ Save `Insert`, whose value field comes before the series it goes into: the series is first.
    Bind series of text or failure to c-fields-in-order unto emitter, given (the node expression, the number first, the number last):
        Define operands as a series of node.
        Define emitted as a series of text.
        Define place as first.
        While place is not greater than last, repeat:
            Define operand as cast field-of on (expression, place).
            Insert operand into operands.
            Define operand-c as cast one's c-of on (operand) or pass the failure off.
            Insert operand-c into emitted.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Define gathered as a series of text with (cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted)).
        For each operand-c in emitted, repeat:
            Insert operand-c into gathered.
        Done.
        Return gathered.
    Done.

    /// A call's arguments as C, each as the kind its parameter wants — wrapped into a union where
    /// the parameter is one. One passed for an interface is the object it is. Gives back what binds
    /// them in order (see `order-prefix`), then the list.
    Bind series of text or failure to c-arguments unto emitter, given (the node parameters, the node handed):
        Define operands as a series of node.
        Define emitted as a series of text.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in handed's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define wanted as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (item place of parameters's children, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define argument-c as "".
            If wanted starts with "interface ", the argument-c becomes cast one's c-of on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            Otherwise, the argument-c becomes cast one's c-of-as on (argument, wanted) or pass the failure off.
            Insert argument into operands.
            Insert argument-c into emitted.
        Done.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted).
        Define listing as "".
        For each argument-c in emitted, repeat:
            If listing is "", the listing becomes argument-c.
            Otherwise, the listing becomes "{listing}, {argument-c}".
        Done.
        Return a series of text with (prefix, listing).
    Done.

    /// An expression as C text, whatever its kind — what `converted to text` and a hole make.
    Bind text or failure to c-text-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast c-text-from on (kind, value) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// A value of a kind, already as C, as C text.
    Bind text or failure to c-text-from, given (the text kind, the text value):
        // A chase's text is a copy: the chase lives on, apart from it.
        If kind is "chase", return "cufet_chase_text({value})".
        If kind is "bits", return cast c-bits-text on (value).
        If cast is-scalar on (kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {kind} as text")).
        If kind is "number", return "cufet_text_from_dec({value})".
        If kind is "fact", return "({value} ? \"true\" : \"false\")".
        Return value.
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to c-binary unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        If cast is-void-test on (expression), return cast one's c-void-test on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define overloaded as cast one's overload-for on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        If overloaded is not void, return cast one's c-overload-call on (expression, overloaded) or pass the failure off.
        If (cast one's is-matrix-binary on (expression) or pass the failure off), return cast one's c-matrix-binary on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define left-side as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        Define left-c as cast one's c-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Define sides as a series of text with (left-c, right-c).
        // `and` and `or` go left to right already, and must not work out their right side when the
        // left decides.
        Define prefix as "".
        If operator is not "And" and operator is not "Or":
            The prefix becomes cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (left-side, cast field-of on (expression, 3)), sides).
        Done.
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, cast one's c-binary-of on (expression, item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides) or pass the failure off).
    Done.

    /// A binary operator over its operands already as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-binary-of unto emitter, given (the node expression, the text left-c, the text right-c):
        Define left-side as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        Define left as left-c.
        Define right as right-c.
        Define at-line as (cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word.
        If (cast one's kind-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off) is "bits":
            Return cast c-bits-binary on (operator, left, right, at-line) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define left-kind as cast one's kind-of on (left-side) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        If (operator is "Equal" or operator is "NotEqual") and (cast is-union on (left-kind) or cast is-union on (right-kind)):
            Return cast one's c-union-equal on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // A voidable compared with a value of what it holds: the value goes in as a voidable, so
        // `void` is unequal to it and a held value is compared as itself.
        If (operator is "Equal" or operator is "NotEqual") and left-kind is not right-kind:
            If cast is-voidable on (left-kind):
                The right becomes cast one's c-coerce on (right, right-kind, left-kind).
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-voidable on (right-kind):
                The left becomes cast one's c-coerce on (left, left-kind, right-kind).
                The left-kind becomes right-kind.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-scalar on (left-kind) is false:
            If operator is "Equal", return "({cast c-equal on (left-kind, left, right)})".
            If operator is "NotEqual", return "(!{cast c-equal on (left-kind, left, right)})".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on a {left-kind}")).
        Done.
        If left-kind is "number":
            Judge operator, where it is:
                "Plus", return "cufet_add({left}, {right})".
                "Minus", return "cufet_sub({left}, {right})".
                "Star", return "cufet_mul({left}, {right})".
                "Slash", return "cufet_div({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
                "Percent", return "cufet_mod({left}, {right}, {at-line})".
                "Equal", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
                "NotEqual", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) != 0)".
                "Lt", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) < 0)".
                "Gt", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) > 0)".
                "Lte", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) <= 0)".
                "Gte", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) >= 0)".
                Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on numbers")).
            Done.
        Done.
        If left-kind is "text":
            If operator is "Equal", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
            If operator is "NotEqual", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) != 0)".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on text")).
        Done.
        Judge operator, where it is:
            "And", return "({left} && {right})".
            "Or", return "({left} || {right})".
            "Xor", return "(!!({left}) != !!({right}))".
            "Equal", return "(!!({left}) == !!({right}))".
            "NotEqual", return "(!!({left}) != !!({right}))".
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on facts")).
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The C type a kind of value is held in.
    Bind text to c-type, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-record on (kind), return cast record-c-name on (kind).
        If cast is-failable on (kind), return cast failable-c-name on (kind).
        If kind is "chase", return "CufetChase*".
        If kind is "matrix", return "CufetMatrix*".
        If kind is "address", return "void*".
        If kind is "rabbit", return "cufet_rabbit".
        If kind is "bits", return "CufetBits".
        If cast is-stream on (kind), return "FILE*".
        If cast is-channel on (kind), return "cufet_chan*".
        If cast is-task-handle on (kind), return "cufet_rbox*".
        If cast is-set on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (kind))}*".
        If cast is-function on (kind), return cast function-c-name on (kind).
        // What a handler has caught: its message — the exception's only part a program can reach.
        If kind is "exception", return "const char*".
        If kind is "failure", return "CufetFailure".
        If cast is-map on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (kind)}*".
        If cast is-mapping on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (cast mapping-map on (kind))}_pair".
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return cast voidable-c-name on (kind).
        If cast is-union on (kind), return cast union-c-name on (kind).
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}*".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind)).
        If kind is "number", return "CufetDec".
        If kind is "fact", return "int".
        Return "const char*".
    Done.

    /// The runtime call that writes a value of a kind, without the line's end.
    Bind text to write-call, given (the text kind, the text value):
        If cast is-record on (kind), return "{cast record-c-name on (kind)}_write({value})".
        If kind is "failure", return "fputs(\"<failure>\", stdout)".
        If kind is "chase", return "cufet_write_text(cufet_chase_show({value}))".
        If kind is "bits", return "cufet_write_bits({value})".
        If kind is "matrix", return "cufet_mat_write({value})".
        // An address prints as what it is, never as its value — two runs get different pointers.
        If kind is "address", return "fputs(\"<address>\", stdout)".
        If kind starts with "axiom ", return "fputs(\"<axiom>\", stdout)".
        // A set prints as the collection it reads as — its elements in the order they went in,
        // spelled as a series is — not as the map it is stored as.
        If cast is-set on (kind):
            Define element-write as cast write-call on (cast set-element on (kind), "cf_sw->vals[cf_si]").
            Return "(\{ {cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (kind))}* cf_sw = {value}; fputs(\"(\", stdout); for (int cf_si = 0; cf_si < cf_sw->len; cf_si++) \{ if (cf_si > 0) fputs(\", \", stdout); {element-write}; \} fputs(\")\", stdout); \})".
        Done.
        // Printed as the object the prelude says it is — one with no fields — as the interpreter does.
        If kind is "rabbit", return "fputs(\"rabbit()\", stdout)".
        If cast is-function on (kind), return "fputs(\"<function>\", stdout)".
        If kind is "exception", return "fputs(\"<exception>\", stdout)".
        If cast is-map on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (kind)}_write({value})".
        If cast is-mapping on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (cast mapping-map on (kind))}_pair_write({value})".
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return "{cast voidable-c-name on (kind)}_write({value})".
        If cast is-union on (kind), return "{cast union-c-name on (kind)}_write({value})".
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}_write({value})".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind))}_write({value})".
        If kind is "number", return "cufet_write_number({value})".
        If kind is "fact", return "cufet_write_fact({value})".
        Return "cufet_write_text({value})".
    Done.

    Bind void to line unto emitter, given (the text written):
        Insert one's indent into one's body.
        Insert written into one's body.
        Insert "\n" into one's body.
    Done.

    /// A block's statements, one level in. What a block defines is gone when it ends, so the kinds
    /// of the names are put back as they were.
    Bind void or failure to emit-block unto emitter, given (the node statements):
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define begun as cast one's opening-scope.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Cast one's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's closing-scope on (begun).
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
    Done.

    /// Whether `left` and `right`, two values of `kind`, are equal — as C.
    Bind text to c-equal, given (the text kind, the text left, the text right):
        // Two maps are equal only when they are one map.
        If cast is-map on (kind), return "({left} == {right})".
        If cast is-record on (kind), return "{cast record-c-name on (kind)}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If kind is "chase", return "cufet_chase_eq({left}, {right})".
        If kind is "rabbit", return "cufet_rabbit_eq({left}, {right})".
        If kind is "bits", return "(({left}).value == ({right}).value)".
        // Two matrices are equal only when they are one matrix, as the interpreter has it.
        If kind is "matrix", return "({left} == {right})".
        If kind is "address", return "({left} == {right})".
        // Two sets are equal only when they are one set, as two maps are.
        If cast is-set on (kind), return "({left} == {right})".
        If cast is-function on (kind), return "(({left}).fn == ({right}).fn && ({left}).env == ({right}).env)".
        If cast is-mapping on (kind), return "{cast map-c-name on (cast mapping-map on (kind))}_pair_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return "{cast voidable-c-name on (kind)}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast is-union on (kind), return "{cast union-c-name on (kind)}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (kind))}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return "{cast c-struct-name on (cast object-of on (kind))}_eq({left}, {right})".
        If kind is "number", return "(cufet_cmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
        If kind is "text", return "(strcmp({left}, {right}) == 0)".
        Return "(!!({left}) == !!({right}))".
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-statement unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        // A store into something older than the rabbit it stands in — see regions.cufe.
        Define escaping as cast one's escapes-to on (statement).
        If escaping is not less than 0:
            Cast one's emit-escaping-store on (statement, escaping) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            "StateStatement":
                Define said as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
                Define value as cast one's c-of on (said) or pass the failure off.
                Define value-kind as cast one's kind-of on (said) or pass the failure off.
                // Locked for the whole line: a `State` is several writes. The value is worked out
                // before the lock is taken — it may wait on a task that prints, which a lock held
                // across the wait would keep from printing for ever.
                Cast one's line on ("\{ __auto_type cf_said = {value}; cufet_out_lock(); {cast write-call on (value-kind, "cf_said")}; cufet_nl(); cufet_out_unlock(); \}").
            Done.
            "DefineStatement":
                If (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s kind is "AxiomLiteral":
                    Cast one's emit-axiom-define on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                    Return.
                Done.
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                // A shared constant is a global, set where its `Define` stands.
                If (the entry for cast place-of-define on (statement) in one's constant-places) is not void:
                    Define shared-kind as the entry for name in one's constants but void is "".
                    Cast one's line on ("{cast c-name on (name)} = {cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), shared-kind) or pass the failure off};").
                    Return.
                Done.
                Define assigned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
                Define value-kind as cast one's kind-of on (assigned) or pass the failure off.
                // Declared with a type, it holds that type — a union, the value wrapped into it.
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) is false:
                    The value-kind becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (assigned, value-kind) or pass the failure off.
                In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes value-kind.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes value-kind.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
                Cast one's declared-here on (name).
                Cast one's line on ("{cast c-type on (value-kind)} {cast c-name on (name)} = {value};").
                Cast one's register-unmade on (name, value-kind).
            Done.
            "BecomesStatement":
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in one's kinds) is void:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the name '{name}', defined where this compiler cannot see it")).
                Done.
                // Into what the name is stored as.
                Define stored as cast one's stored-kind on (name).
                Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), stored) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("{cast c-name on (name)} = {value};").
                In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes stored.
                In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
            Done.
            "IfStatement":
                Cast one's emit-if on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "WhileStatement":
                Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("while ({condition}) \{").
                Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
                Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
                Cast one's line on ("\}").
            Done.
            "RepeatUntilStatement":
                Cast one's line on ("do \{").
                Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
                Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
                Define condition as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's line on ("\} while (!({condition}));").
            Done.
            "ReturnStatement":
                // Inside a task, a `Return` publishes to its box.
                If (the entry for "%task" in one's kinds) is not void:
                    Cast one's emit-task-return on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                    Return.
                Done.
                Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
                Define gives as the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "".
                If cast is-nothing on (returned):
                    If gives is "failure of void", cast one's line on (cast one's c-return on ("cfl_void_done()")).
                    Otherwise, cast one's line on (cast one's c-return on ("")).
                Done.
                // A lambda's first pass, working out what it gives back.
                Otherwise if gives is "?":
                    Cast one's line on ("return {cast one's noted-return on (returned) or pass the failure off};").
                Done.
                Otherwise, cast one's line on (cast one's c-return on (cast one's c-of-as on (returned, gives) or pass the failure off)).
            Done.
            "CastStatement":
                // An axiom run for what it does; what it gives back is dropped.
                If (cast keyed-field on (statement, ":RunsAxiom")) is not void:
                    Cast one's line on ("(void)({cast one's c-axiom-call on (statement) or pass the failure off});").
                    Return.
                Done.
                Define call as cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, 2))).
                // `… or pass the failure off.`, or inside a `Try`, where a failure goes to the handler.
                Define passes-off as the number of statement's children is greater than 5 and (cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word is ":PassesFailureOff".
                Cast one's emit-failable-cast on (call, passes-off) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "BindStatement", cast one's emit-local-bind on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            // An interface was gathered with the program's declarations, and builds nothing itself.
            "InterfaceDefinition", return.
            // A pull's functions and objects are the program's, gathered with its own; what is left
            // is a block. A region frees nothing yet — see emit-pulled.
            "PullStatement", cast one's emit-pulled on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "PullRabbitStatement", cast one's emit-rabbit on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "ObjectDefinition", return a failure (cast not-built on ("an object defined inside a body")).
            "PossessiveSetStatement", cast one's emit-field-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "StopStatement", cast one's line on (cast one's c-loop-jump on ("break")).
            "ExitStatement":
                Define status as "cufet_dec_from_ll(0)".
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is false:
                    The status becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Cast one's line on ("cufet_exit({status}, {(cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s word});").
            Done.
            "SkipStatement", cast one's line on (cast one's c-loop-jump on ("continue")).
            "SuppressStatement":
                Define handler as the entry for "%suppress" in one's kinds but void is "".
                Cast one's line on ("\{ cf_sup_{handler} = 1; goto cf_done_{handler}; \}").
            Done.
            "JudgeStatement", cast one's emit-judge on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "TryStatement", cast one's emit-try on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "FileWriteStatement", cast one's emit-file-write on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "WithOpenStatement", cast one's emit-with-open on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "SendStatement", cast one's emit-send on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "PipeExpression":
                If cast is-task-pipe on (statement), cast one's emit-task-pipe on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Otherwise, cast one's emit-run-pipe on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            "OutputStatement", cast one's emit-output on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "ForEachFromInputStatement", cast one's emit-from-input on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            // `Yield.` — an interrupt checkpoint; the operating system hands out the turns.
            "YieldStatement", cast one's line on ("cufet_checkpoint();").
            "AcknowledgeInterruptStatement", cast one's line on ("cufet_interrupted = 0;").
            "CloseStatement", cast one's emit-close on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "LaunchTaskStatement", cast one's emit-launch on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "WriteToStreamStatement", cast one's emit-stream-write on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "MapSetStatement", cast one's emit-map-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "MatrixSetStatement", cast one's emit-matrix-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "SeedChanceStatement", cast one's emit-seed on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "RecordNamedSetStatement", cast one's emit-record-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            "ForEachStatement" or "SeriesInsertStatement" or "SeriesRemoveAtStatement" or "SeriesRemoveValueStatement"
                    or "SeriesSetStatement":
                Cast one's emit-series-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `unbury <stash>` as the call it is: the checker has rewritten every burying function into one
    /// that hands back a closure, so resuming a stash is calling that closure with nothing.
    Bind node to as-resumed, given (the node expression):
        Return cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast listed)).
    Done.

    /// Whether a pull opens a region — it pulls an object that says `and region`.
    Bind fact to pulls-region unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        For each pulled in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define definition as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pulled, 1)) in one's objects.
            If definition is not void:
                For each conformed in (cast field-of on (definition, 8))'s children, repeat:
                    If cast unquoted on (conformed) is "region", return true.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// `Pull … Done.` — a block, with the functions and objects in it gathered as the program's.
    /// ⚠ `Pull a rabbit.` is a region, and a region here FREES NOTHING yet: a value made in it and
    /// kept outside it — copied out by C#, which the checked tree does not say — would otherwise be
    /// read after it was freed. Kept, it costs memory and never changes what a program prints.
    Bind void or failure to emit-pulled unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        // A region of the writer's own is a rabbit by another name: the same arena, freed the same way.
        If cast one's pulls-region on (statement):
            Cast one's emit-region on (statement, "") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define begun as cast one's opening-scope.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If cast declares-only on (inner) is false:
                Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's closing-scope on (begun).
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// Whether a statement only declares — gathered with the program's declarations, and built there.
    Bind fact to declares-only, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        Return kind is "BindStatement" or kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition"
            or kind is "GetterDeclaration" or kind is "SetterDeclaration" or kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration"
            or kind is "UnmakerDeclaration".
    Done.

    /// Where a `Define` stands, as the key its constant is known by.
    Bind text to place-of-define, given (the node statement):
        Return "{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s word}".
    Done.

    /// The bundled books with a Cufet layer this compiler can build from source.
    Bind series of text to layered-books:
        Return a series of text with ("math", "chance", "collections", "regex").
    Done.

    /// Whether a program names something — a book it calls, say — anywhere in it.
    Bind fact to names-anywhere, given (the node tree, the text name):
        If tree's kind is "VariableReference" and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) is name, return true.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If child's kind is not "atom" and cast names-anywhere on (child, name), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The statements hoisting reaches: the top level and every pull's body, rabbits' included.
    Bind void to gather-hoisted, given (the node statements, the series of node found):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Insert statement into found.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement" or statement's kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast gather-hoisted on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), found).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `Judge <subject>, where it is:` over values — the subject held as `it`, each arm a test of it
    /// against its values, in order. An arm naming a type waits for a later slice.
    Bind void or failure to emit-judge unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define subject as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (subject) or pass the failure off.
        Define subject-kind as cast one's kind-of on (subject) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-union on (subject-kind):
            Cast one's emit-judge-union on (statement, subject-kind) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-scalar on (subject-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("judging a {subject-kind}")).
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("{cast c-type on (subject-kind)} cv_it = {value};").
        In one's kinds, the entry for "it" becomes subject-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%it" becomes subject-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@it" becomes "".
        Define first-arm as true.
        For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If the number of (cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children is greater than 0:
                Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a judgement arm naming a type")).
            Done.
            Define tests as "".
            For each written in (cast field-of on (arm, 5))'s children, repeat:
                Define written-kind as cast one's kind-of on (written) or pass the failure off.
                If written-kind is not subject-kind:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a judgement arm of another kind than its subject")).
                Done.
                Define test as cast c-equal on (subject-kind, "cv_it", cast one's c-of on (written) or pass the failure off).
                If tests is "", the tests becomes test.
                Otherwise, the tests becomes "{tests} || {test}".
            Done.
            If first-arm, cast one's line on ("if ({tests}) \{").
            Otherwise, cast one's line on ("\} else if ({tests}) \{").
            The first-arm becomes false.
            Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (arm, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false:
            If first-arm:
                Cast one's line on ("\{").
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast one's line on ("\} else \{").
            Done.
            Cast one's emit-block on (otherwise-body) or pass the failure off.
            The first-arm becomes false.
        Done.
        If first-arm is false, cast one's line on ("\}").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.

    /// What this compiler cannot build in a function yet — anything marked — or "". A method bound
    /// `unto` an object is built as that object's; a maker is a function giving back its object.
    Bind text or failure to function-beyond, given (the node statement):
        // A pattern is lowered to a function that hands it to the `regex` book's engine, and a
        // `cufet` axiom that says what it gives back to the function it holds — both ordinary.
        If the number of statement's children is greater than 8:
            If cast is-lowered-axiom on (statement), return "".
            Return "a Bind with {(cast field-of on (statement, 9))'s word}".
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Whether a `Bind` was lowered from an axiom into an ordinary function — a pattern, or a
    /// `cufet` axiom; the mark is left only so the checker can ask for the book.
    Bind fact to is-lowered-axiom, given (the node statement):
        If the number of statement's children is not greater than 9, return false.
        If (cast field-of on (statement, 9))'s word is not ":FromAxiomLanguage", return false.
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 10)).
        Return language is "regex" or language is "cufet".
    Done.

    /// A function's head as C: what it gives back, its name, and its parameters.
    /// `overrides` gives a parameter the kind a copy of the function was asked for; `named` is the
    /// copy's C name, or "" for the function's own.
    Bind text or failure to c-signature unto emitter, given (the node statement, the map from text to text overrides, the text named):
        Define gives as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define head as "void".
        If gives is not "void", the head becomes cast c-type on (gives).
        Define listing as "".
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define overridden as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) in overrides.
            If overridden is not void, the taken becomes overridden.
            If taken is "void", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a parameter of no type")).
            Define one-parameter as "{cast c-type on (taken)} {cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)))}".
            If listing is "", the listing becomes one-parameter.
            Otherwise, the listing becomes "{listing}, {one-parameter}".
        Done.
        If listing is "", the listing becomes "void".
        Define function-c as named.
        If function-c is "", the function-c becomes cast c-function-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))).
        Return "{head} {function-c}({listing})".
    Done.

    /// One function as C. A body sees its parameters and nothing of the program's top level.
    Bind text or failure to c-function unto emitter, given (the node statement, the map from text to text overrides, the text named):
        Define writer as cast one's sibling.
        Cast writer's line on (cast writer's frame-start).
        In writer's kinds, the entry for "%return" becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast writer's feed-stage on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))).
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define overridden as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) in overrides.
            If overridden is not void, the taken becomes overridden.
            In writer's kinds, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) becomes taken.
        Done.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            Cast writer's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast writer's close-failable.
        Define signature as cast one's c-signature on (statement, overrides, named) or pass the failure off.
        Return "{signature} \{\n{writer's body converted to text}\}\n\n".
    Done.

    /// The whole program as one C file: the series types, its objects, its functions and methods —
    /// declared first, so any may call any — then what it does.
    Bind text or failure to c-program, given (the node program, the text prelude-folder):
        Define functions as a map from text to node.
        Define objects as a map from text to node.
        Define methods as a map from text to node.
        // Every method, by the object it belongs to: written inside it, or bound `unto` it.
        Define owned as a series of node.
        Define owners as a series of text.
        Define hoisted as a series of node.
        // A bundled book the program calls is built from its own source, as a module is — its
        // constants set before anything runs, as the prelude's are.
        Define book-constants as a series of node.
        For each book in cast layered-books, repeat:
            // A pattern names no book: it calls the `regex` book's engine by its hidden name.
            If cast names-anywhere on (program, book) or cast names-anywhere on (program, "match in {book}"):
                Define layer as cast listed.
                Try to:
                    The layer becomes cast parser's program-tree on (read all from the file "{prelude-folder}/{book}.cufe").
                Done.
                In case of failure:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the {book} book, which could not be read")).
                Done.
                // Its helpers hidden after it, as the loader hides a bundled book's.
                Cast checker's make-private on (layer, book, a map from text to text, true, a map from text to text).
                For each statement in layer's children, repeat:
                    Insert statement into hoisted.
                    If statement's kind is "DefineStatement", insert statement into book-constants.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast gather-hoisted on (program, hoisted).
        Define interfaces as a map from text to node.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
                In interfaces, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes statement.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                Define beyond as cast object-beyond on (statement).
                If beyond is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond)).
                Define object-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                In objects, the entry for object-name becomes statement.
                For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                    Define beyond-method as cast function-beyond on (method) or pass the failure off.
                    If beyond-method is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond-method)).
                    In methods, the entry for "{object-name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}" becomes method.
                    Insert method into owned.
                    Insert object-name into owners.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement":
                Define beyond as cast function-beyond on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                If beyond is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (beyond)).
                Define unto-target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
                If cast is-nothing on (unto-target):
                    In functions, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes statement.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Define object-name as cast unquoted on (unto-target).
                    If (the entry for object-name in objects) is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a method bound 'unto' {object-name}")).
                    In methods, the entry for "{object-name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))}" becomes statement.
                    Insert statement into owned.
                    Insert object-name into owners.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define writer as cast fresh-emitter on (functions, objects, methods, interfaces).
        If cast uses-tasks on (program), in writer's inferred, the entry for "%tasks" becomes "yes".
        // Getters, by the object they read: written inside it, or bound `unto` it.
        Define getters as a series of node.
        Define getter-owners as a series of text.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                For each getter in (cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s children, repeat:
                    Insert getter into getters.
                    Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) into getter-owners.
                Done.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "GetterDeclaration" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) is false:
                Insert statement into getters.
                Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)) into getter-owners.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define getter-place as 0.
        For each getter in getters, repeat:
            Increment getter-place by 1.
            In methods, the entry for "{item getter-place of getter-owners}'s getter {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1))}" becomes getter.
        Done.
        // Setters the same way: written inside the object, or bound `unto` it.
        Define setters as a series of node.
        Define setter-owners as a series of text.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                For each setter in (cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s children, repeat:
                    Insert setter into setters.
                    Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) into setter-owners.
                Done.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "SetterDeclaration" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) is false:
                Insert statement into setters.
                Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) into setter-owners.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define setter-place as 0.
        For each setter in setters, repeat:
            Increment setter-place by 1.
            In methods, the entry for "{item setter-place of setter-owners}'s setter {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (setter, 1))}" becomes setter.
        Done.
        // Operator overloads, each by its operator and its ordered pair of operand types.
        Define overloads as a series of node.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration":
                Insert statement into overloads.
                // Noted before any body is written, so every operator in one may ask.
                In writer's inferred, the entry for "%overloads" becomes "yes".
                In methods, the entry for cast overload-key on ((cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word,
                    cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)), cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5))) becomes statement.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast writer's register-pulled-modules on (hoisted).
        // Unmakers, each by its object — noted before any body is written, so every `Define` may ask.
        Cast writer's note-unmakers on (hoisted).
        // Foreign source: whether there is any, whether anything it acquires is given back, and the
        // source an axiom with no result is — pasted above everything that may call into it.
        Cast writer's note-foreign on (program, hoisted).
        // What every pipe stage is fed — told before any stage's body is written.
        Cast writer's note-pipes on (program) or pass the failure off.
        // Which functions bound inside a body are written together, and so see one another.
        Cast writer's note-groups on (program).
        // Every shared constant: a `permanently` the hoist reaches, its kind known before any body is.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement" and (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s word is "true":
                Define constant-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define constant-kind as "".
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) is false:
                    The constant-kind becomes cast writer's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    The constant-kind becomes cast writer's kind-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                In writer's constants, the entry for constant-name becomes constant-kind.
                In writer's constant-places, the entry for cast place-of-define on (statement) becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pair in objects, repeat:
            Define conformance as cast writer's conformance-beyond on (the value of pair).
            If conformance is not "", return a failure (cast not-built on (conformance)).
        Done.

        // The objects, each after those its fields hold.
        Define ordered as a series of text.
        Define already-ordered as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in objects, repeat:
            Cast writer's order-objects on (the key of pair, already-ordered, a map from text to fact, ordered) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        // Each object's series type named first, then the structs, then what writes and compares
        // them, then each series of objects whole — so a node may hold a series of nodes.
        Define structs as a chase.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on ("object {object-name}").
            Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast writer's c-object-struct on (object-name) or pass the failure off into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast c-object-heads on (object-name) into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast c-series-helpers on ("object {object-name}") into structs.
        Done.
        For each object-name in ordered, repeat:
            Insert cast writer's c-object on (object-name) or pass the failure off into structs.
        Done.

        Define declared as a chase.
        Define defined as a chase.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                // One that takes an interface is built only as the copies its calls ask for.
                Define interface-taking as cast writer's takes-interface on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                If interface-taking is false:
                    Insert "{cast writer's c-signature on (statement, a map from text to text, "") or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
                    Insert cast writer's c-function on (statement, a map from text to text, "") or pass the failure off into defined.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define getter-index as 0.
        For each getter in getters, repeat:
            Increment getter-index by 1.
            Define getter-owner as item getter-index of getter-owners.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-getter-signature on (getter-owner, getter) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-getter on (getter-owner, getter) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        For each overload in overloads, repeat:
            Insert "{cast writer's c-overload-signature on (overload) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-overload on (overload) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        For each statement in hoisted, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "UnmakerDeclaration":
                Insert "{cast c-unmaker-signature on (statement)};\n" into declared.
                Insert cast writer's c-unmaker on (statement) or pass the failure off into defined.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define setter-index as 0.
        For each setter in setters, repeat:
            Increment setter-index by 1.
            Define setter-owner as item setter-index of setter-owners.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-setter-signature on (setter-owner, setter) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-setter on (setter-owner, setter) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each method in owned, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define owner as item place of owners.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-method-signature on (owner, method) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-method on (owner, method) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        // A book's constants first, as the prelude runs before the program.
        For each constant in book-constants, repeat:
            Cast writer's emit-statement on (constant) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            If cast declares-only on (statement) is false:
                Cast writer's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Every copy a call asked for — a copy's own calls may ask for more.
        Define built-copies as 0.
        While built-copies is less than the number of writer's pending-functions, repeat:
            Increment built-copies by 1.
            Define copied as item built-copies of writer's pending-functions.
            Define copy-name as item built-copies of writer's pending-names.
            Define copy-kinds as item built-copies of writer's pending-kinds.
            Insert "{cast writer's c-signature on (copied, copy-kinds, copy-name) or pass the failure off};\n" into declared.
            Insert cast writer's c-function on (copied, copy-kinds, copy-name) or pass the failure off into defined.
        Done.
        // Every union the program used, each with its series, and every voidable of an object or a
        // union — after the objects they may hold. Then the shared constants, now every type is whole.
        Define union-types as a chase.
        For each union in writer's union-order, repeat:
            // Copy families are written after every type, below.
            If cast copied-kind on (union) is not "", skip.
            // A series of series, or of voidables: the series that holds them.
            If cast held-element on (union) is not "":
                Insert cast c-series-helpers on (cast held-element on (union)) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-voidable on (union):
                Insert cast c-voidable-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-map on (union):
                Insert cast c-map-helpers on (union) into union-types.
                Insert cast c-series-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-function on (union):
                // One an object may hold is written ahead of the objects instead.
                If cast is-early-function on (union) is false, insert cast c-function-helpers on (union) into union-types.
                Insert cast c-series-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-failable on (union):
                Insert cast c-failable-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast is-record on (union):
                Insert cast c-record-helpers on (union) into union-types.
                Insert cast c-series-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Insert cast c-union-helpers on (union) into union-types.
                Insert cast c-series-helpers on (union) into union-types.
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert cast writer's c-copy-families or pass the failure off into union-types.
        For each written in writer's lambda-types, repeat:
            Insert written into union-types.
        Done.
        For each pair in writer's constants, repeat:
            Insert "static {cast c-type on (the value of pair)} {cast c-name on (the key of pair)};\n" into union-types.
        Done.
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "#include \"cufet-runtime.h\"\n\n" into out.
        // What foreign source needs above it — beside the runtime's header, in the runtime folder.
        If (the entry for "%foreign" in writer's inferred) is not void, insert "#include \"cufet-foreign.h\"\n\n" into out.
        Insert cast c-series-prelude into out.
        Insert cast c-chase-runtime into out.
        Insert cast c-voidable-prelude into out.
        // A series of a union named ahead of the objects, which may hold one by its address — and
        // how it is written and compared, which an object's own writing calls.
        For each union in writer's union-order, repeat:
            If cast copied-kind on (union) is not "", skip.
            // A series of series or of voidables, named ahead so an object may hold one by its address.
            If cast held-element on (union) is not "":
                Define held-series as cast series-c-name on (cast held-element on (union)).
                Insert "typedef struct {held-series}_s {held-series};\n" into out.
                Skip.
            Done.
            If cast is-voidable on (union) or cast is-failable on (union) or cast is-function on (union) or union starts with "thunk:", skip.
            // A map is held by its address, so an object may hold one named this far ahead.
            If cast is-map on (union):
                Insert "typedef struct {cast map-c-name on (union)}_s {cast map-c-name on (union)};\n" into out.
                Insert "static void {cast map-c-name on (union)}_write({cast map-c-name on (union)}* m);\n" into out.
                // And a series of them, which an object may hold too.
                Insert "typedef struct cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}_s cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)};\n" into out.
                Insert "static void cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}_write(cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}* s);\n" into out.
                Insert "static int cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}_eq(cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}* a, cser_{cast map-c-name on (union)}* b);\n" into out.
                Skip.
            Done.
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (union).
            Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into out.
            Insert "static void {series-type}_write({series-type}* s);\n" into out.
            Insert "static int {series-type}_eq({series-type}* a, {series-type}* b);\n" into out.
        Done.
        For each union in writer's union-order, repeat:
            If cast is-function on (union) and cast is-early-function on (union), insert cast c-function-helpers on (union) into out.
        Done.
        Insert structs converted to text into out.
        Insert union-types converted to text into out.
        Insert declared converted to text into out.
        For each written in writer's lambda-protos, repeat:
            Insert written into out.
        Done.
        Insert "\n" into out.
        Insert defined converted to text into out.
        For each written in writer's lambda-code, repeat:
            Insert written into out.
        Done.
        Insert "int main(int argc, char** argv) \{\n" into out.
        Insert "    cufet_set_args(argc, argv);\n" into out.
        Insert "    CUFET_STDOUT_BINARY();\n" into out.
        Insert "    cufet_watch_stack();\n" into out.
        Define has-tasks as (the entry for "%tasks" in writer's inferred) is not void.
        If has-tasks or cast uses-interrupts on (program), insert cast c-main-signals on (has-tasks) into out.
        Insert "    cufet_arena_push();\n" into out.
        Insert "    {cast writer's frame-start}\n" into out.
        Insert writer's body converted to text into out.
        Insert "    cufet_arena_pop();\n" into out.
        Insert "    return 0;\n" into out.
        Insert "\}\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.
Done.
